23244.3 gpu: world feature feature=bumpmap declared=57 visible=52 resolved=57 missing=0 first=NATURE/BLENDGROUNDTOGRASS008 resource=materials/Nature/dirtground001_height-ssbump.vtf reason=the materials name 31 distinct $bumpmap textures, so the one sampler slot the pass started with cannot apply each material's own; per-material binding is the --world-material-bump switch, and with it on the 16 that do not set $ssbump sample their own tile through a texinfo-axis tangent basis while the 41 that do stay refused (see the $ssbump row)
23244.3 gpu: world feature feature=bumpmap2 declared=1 visible=1 resolved=1 missing=0 first=COALMINES/BLENDGROUNDTOGRASS_COALMINES resource=materials/Nature/dirtground003_height-ssbump.vtf reason=$bumpmap2 is layer 2's normal map: it is lerped into layer 1's normal by the vertex blend weight, so it is sampled only when --world-material-bump and --world-bump2 are both on; with either off it is refused, not silently replaced by layer 1's; 1/1 of those materials also declare $ssbump, so their second-layer texel is a bumpBasis weight and stays refused even with both switches on (--world-bump2-texture measures the layer with a diagnostic normal map instead)
23244.3 gpu: world feature feature=ssbump declared=41 visible=38 resolved=41 missing=0 first=NATURE/BLENDGROUNDTOGRASS008 resource=Nature/dirtground001_height-ssbump reason=$ssbump selects `BUMPMAP == 2`, where the texel is not a signed normal but three bumpBasis weights against three lightmap directions; this pass samples one lightmap and one tangent-space normal, so these materials are refused by name even when --world-material-bump is on
23244.3 gpu: world feature feature=detail declared=53 visible=50 resolved=0 missing=53 first=WOOD/WOOD_BEAM02 resource=materials/overlays/detail006.vmt reason=detail layers are the --world-detail switch: the detail material's $basetexture is sampled at the atlas uv scaled by $detailscale and combined with the albedo by $detailblendmode; with the switch off the layer is refused
23244.3 gpu: world feature-detail distinctBumpPaths=31 detailTypesRead=1 firstDetailType=tf_forest_grass
23306.5 gpu: world lighting dynamic=0 specular=0 bump=0 requestedDynamic=0 requestedSpecular=0 requestedBump=0 bumpOwner=WOOD/WOOD_BRIDGE002 bumpTexture=- bumpTextureSource=none bumpOwnerDeclared=0
23306.5 gpu: world lighting-summary controls=6 applied=0 refused=4 disabled=2 notDeclared=0 phong=0(visible 0, exponents 0/0) bumpOwner=WOOD/WOOD_BRIDGE002
23306.5 gpu: world feature-apply bump enabled=0 tiles=0 materials=0 vertices=0 bump2 enabled=0 tiles=0 materials=0 vertices=0 weights=0(-1.000..-1.000) detail enabled=0 tiles=0 materials=0 vertices=0
23306.5 gpu: world lighting-control control=dynamicLighting kind=pass-switch state=disabled declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=131 triangles=184887 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=a pass constant, not a material key: the pixel shader replaces the lightmap-only factor with 0.62+0.38*dot(normal, lightDirection) for 131 visible materials / 184887 visible triangles; no VMT declares it, so every surface is shaded by the same guessed direction and the baked lightmap's own direct light is counted twice; off
23306.5 gpu: world lighting-control control=specular kind=pass-switch state=disabled declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=131 triangles=184887 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=a pass constant: one lobe (boost 0.12, exponent 32) for 131 visible materials / 184887 visible triangles; no visible material declares $phong, so the lobe is added to materials that never asked for one; off
23306.5 gpu: world lighting-control control=bump kind=pass-switch state=refused declared=57 visible=52 resolved=57 missing=0 materials=52 triangles=32901 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=NATURE/BLENDGROUNDTOGRASS008 resource=materials/Nature/dirtground001_height-ssbump.vtf reason=off: the world pass has one bump sampler slot (--world-bump) and the per-material path is off too (--world-material-bump), so the 52 visible materials that name one of 31 distinct $bumpmap textures are drawn with no normal map at all
23306.5 gpu: world lighting-control control=$bumpmap2 kind=material-key state=refused declared=1 visible=1 resolved=1 missing=0 materials=1 triangles=1024 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=COALMINES/BLENDGROUNDTOGRASS_COALMINES resource=materials/Nature/dirtground003_height-ssbump.vtf reason=$bumpmap2 is layer 2's normal map: it is lerped into layer 1's normal by the vertex blend weight, so it is sampled only when --world-material-bump and --world-bump2 are both on; with either off it is refused, not silently replaced by layer 1's; 1/1 of those materials also declare $ssbump, so their second-layer texel is a bumpBasis weight and stays refused even with both switches on (--world-bump2-texture measures the layer with a diagnostic normal map instead)
23306.6 gpu: world lighting-control control=%detailtype kind=material-key state=refused declared=53 visible=50 resolved=0 missing=53 materials=50 triangles=32958 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=WOOD/WOOD_BEAM02 resource=materials/overlays/detail006.vmt reason=detail layers are the --world-detail switch: the detail material's $basetexture is sampled at the atlas uv scaled by $detailscale and combined with the albedo by $detailblendmode; with the switch off the layer is refused; 53 of 53 referenced detail VMTs are absent from this install, so the layer's own texture and blend mode cannot be resolved here; %detailtype is a key in the material that names the layer, not in the detail VMT, and is read above; 1 material names a %detailtype group (first=tf_forest_grass); %detailtype names a detail-prop group that VBSP consumes at map compile time (it emits prop_detail sprites and models there), so the key never reaches a runtime shader and has no consumer here
23306.6 gpu: world lighting-control control=$ssbump kind=material-key state=refused declared=41 visible=38 resolved=41 missing=0 materials=38 triangles=31634 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=NATURE/BLENDGROUNDTOGRASS008 resource=Nature/dirtground001_height-ssbump reason=$ssbump selects `BUMPMAP == 2`, where the texel is not a signed normal but three bumpBasis weights against three lightmap directions; this pass samples one lightmap and one tangent-space normal, so these materials are refused by name even when --world-material-bump is on
